nd 2) were determined by using the shake-flask method and UU-Vis spectrometer. The 1-octanol used in this experiment was pre-saturated with de-ionized water by overnight incubation with shaking a biphasic mixture of the two at room temperature. A 4 mL solution of the compound (ca. 50 μM) was prepared in pre-saturated octanol and 2 mL was used to record UV-Vis spectrum (250-900nm). The remaining 2 mL solution was incubated with 2 mL water in a 5 mL tube. The tube was covered with aluminium foil and vigorously shaken for 2 h using an automated shaker at 37 °C. The tube was then allowed to stand for 15 min and two layers were separated carefully. The octanol layer was used to record UV-Vis spectrum (250 to 900 nm). The log P values were determined using the following formula: Log P = Log(Absorption at 2 h in octanol / (Absorption at 0 h in octanol - Absorption at 2 h in octanol)). The log P value of cisplatin was measured following a similar procedure except for platinum concentration in aqueous and octanol layer was quantified using ICP-MS. All the experiments were carried out in triplicate."}],"ccdc":["ZASQUJ"]}